-- title:
--   Freeness of the ordinary Σ-corner at level Mr
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring that is a domain, complete for its maximal ideal and has finite residue field, and let $p$ be an odd prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over the residue field, factoring through a finite extension and absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $M \neq 0$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2 \nmid M$. Let $S_{\min} \subseteq S$ contain $p$ and satisfy: for primes $q \neq p$, $q \in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (some element of some inertia subgroup over $q$ acts non-trivially); every $q \in S_{\min}$ with $q \neq p$ divides $M$; every prime $q \neq p$ outside $S_{\min}$ dividing $M$ divides $M$ exactly to order at least two; no $q \neq p$ has $q^3 \mid M$ when $q^2 \mid M$; inertia at each $q \in S_{\min}$, $q \neq p$, acts on $\bar\rho$ with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ if $p \mid M$ (a decomposition-stable free rank-one line on which inertia acts trivially modulo the line). Let $r$ be an auxiliary prime with $r \notin S$, $r \nmid M$, $p \nmid r-1$, such that for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $r$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $r$ one has $(\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma))^2 \neq (r+1)^2$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(M)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by forms with integral $q$-expansions, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ to the residue field such that for all primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Put $L = Mr$ (non-zero, divisible by $r$) and let $H \leq (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $\mathbb Z/r$. Let $\mathbb T$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, acting $\mathcal O$-compatibly on $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{ab}}, \mathcal O)$, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_j$ exhausting the maximal spectrum, $e_j \in \mathfrak m_{j'}$ iff $j \neq j'$) and $i$ an index, with the corner submodule $e_i \cdot H^1$ finite and free over $\mathcal O$. Let $t_{\mathrm{full}}$ and $c_{\mathrm{full}}$ assign to each Hecke generator $T_\ell$, $U_q$, $\langle d\rangle$ at level $L$ away from $S$ an element of $\mathbb T$, respectively of $\mathcal O$. Call a generator guarded if it is not $U_q$ for a prime $q \mid L$ with $q \nmid M$. Assume: every element of $\mathbb T$ acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the operators `opFamily` of the guarded generators; $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ acts as `opFamily` $g$ for guarded $g$; $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g) - c_{\mathrm{full}}(g) \in \mathfrak m_i$ for guarded $g$; any $v \in H^1$ for which, for each guarded $g$ and each $k$, some power $(t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g))^n$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k H^1$, lies in the corner submodule; the residue of $c_{\mathrm{full}}(T_\ell)$ is $\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell \nmid L$ outside $S$; $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q) \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ for primes $q \mid L$ with $q \mid M$, $q \neq p$, $q^2 \mid M$; $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_p)$ is a unit when $p \mid L$ and $p \mid M$; and $c_{\mathrm{full}}(\langle d\rangle) \equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Assume further that the corner submodule is non-zero, that the corner ring at $i$ acts faithfully on it, and that there is an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from the corner ring to the local Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeLocal M S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) under which $e^{-1}$ of the image of $T_\ell$ acts on the corner submodule as the Hecke operator `heckeT L H ℓ 𝒪` for all primes $\ell \nmid L$ outside $S$. Then the corner submodule $e_i \cdot H^1$ is free as a module over the corner ring at $i$.
--
--   This is the multiplicity-one assertion for the ordinary $\Sigma$-corner at the Taylor–Wiles level $L = Mr$: the relevant piece of the cohomology of $\Gamma_H(Mr)$ is free over its local Hecke ring. It feeds the saturation statement [`CohCarrier.saturated_torsionBySet_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.saturated_torsionBySet_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul) and the corresponding freeness statement over [`CuspForm.heckeLocal`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), which are the inputs used when patching at auxiliary primes.
